# Conventional Commits

Follow **[Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/)** when authoring **commit messages** and **pull request titles** (including messages proposed before `git commit` or `gh pr create`).

## Subject line (required)

```
<type>[optional scope]: <short description>
```

- **type** (common): `feat` | `fix` | `docs` | `style` | `refactor` | `perf` | `test` | `build` | `ci` | `chore`
- **scope** (optional): area touched—e.g. `scan`, `catalog`, `search`, `ui`, `ci`, `deps`
- **description**: imperative mood (“add”, not “added”); no trailing period in the subject line; aim for ~72 characters or less.

### Breaking changes

- Append `!` after the type/scope: `feat(catalog)!: change embedding table layout`
- Or put `BREAKING CHANGE:` in the **footer** (after a blank line below the body).

## Body (optional)

- Blank line after the subject.
- Explain *what* and *why*, not paste-only diffs.
- Wrap at ~72 chars for readability.

## Footer (optional)

- Issue references: `Closes #123`
- Co-authorship only when accurate.

## Examples for this codebase

```text
feat(scan): add vector match result screen

feat(catalog): build bundled catalog from CSV

fix(scan): gate low-confidence matches as best guesses

ci: run lint, typecheck, and tests on pull requests

chore(deps): bump expo-router
```

## Pull request titles (required)

Use the **same subject format** as commits:

```text
<type>[optional scope]: <short description>
```

- Put story id and context in the **PR description**, not the title.
- Prefer the same type/scope as the branch and primary commit when the PR is a single feature.

## Agent behavior

When preparing a commit or **`gh pr create --title`** for this project, **default to this format** unless the user specifies otherwise.
